// Two glob-imported modules export the same symbol `shared_value`, and the
// importer uses the bare name. This is an unresolvable ambiguity: the compiler
// must report a collision/ambiguity error rather than silently resolving it.
//
// Today it does neither cleanly -- `merge_into` resolves colliding imported
// symbols first-wins with no diagnostic (namespace.py:722-739), and codegen then
// emits both module functions under the same LLVM name, crashing with a
// DuplicatedNameError Python traceback. Correct behavior is a proper "ambiguous"
// diagnostic at check time. Structural issue in namespace.py merge_into.
// See todo_jul26.md "Structural issues" (merge_into resolves collisions first-wins).
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: ambiguous
// XFAIL: colliding imported symbols are not diagnosed; the duplicate name crashes codegen instead of raising an ambiguity error

import modules.collide_a.*
import modules.collide_b.*

func main() {
    print(shared_value())
}
